    "knowledge_point": "Determining Whether a Right Riemann Sum is an Overestimate or Underestimate",
    "problem": "A right Riemann sum is used to approximate the area under the curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=1$ for each of the functions below. For which function does the Riemann sum give an *underestimate* of the area?",
    "worked_solution": "The right Riemann sum underestimates the area under the respective curve if the function is decreasing over the given interval. \n\nOf the given options, the only function that is decreasing over $x\\in [-1,1]$ is as follows.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039366/assets/bd25af02c775675398a93df167cce72fa3ec50efe7bddb5c92bc7176571ee4dc.png)",
